      {
        "title": "Show HN: Fakeipedia – Wikipedia for worlds that don't exist",
        "link": "https://fakeipedia.org",
        "description": "<p>Hi HN!<p>Fakeipedia is an automatic world-building platform which takes an imagined world and makes a whole wiki that you can endlessly explore by clicking red links.<p>I came up with this idea a few months ago after playing around with worldbuilding in Gemini, but I didn't want to release it until a powerful enough model could do it justice, and I decided that Argon is creative enough to write articles that are worth reading. I was surprised how well it turned out and how engaging some of the writing actually is.<p>If you want to generate an article there is a nominal charge attached ($0.90), which helps cover AI/Stripe costs, and I think I just about break even. You can also steer the generation ala choose-your-own-adventure books when generating a new article. Everything generated is free and public for everyone to see.<p>I hope you like it and I'm very much open to hearing about new world ideas/features that would make this project better.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50126334\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50126334</a></p>\n<p>Points: 8</p>\n<p># Comments: 2</p>",
        "pubDate": "Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:52:04 +0000",
        "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50126334"
      },
